error[V0108]: unsupported Rust signature: `ext::longer` cannot be called from Varyk
 --> crates/varyk/tests/fixtures/errors/v0108_two_reference_parameters/main.vr:6:20
  |
6 |     println!("{}", ext::longer(a, b));
  |                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ unsupported Rust signature: `ext::longer` cannot be called from Varyk
  |
  = note: the Rust signature is `fn longer(a: &str, b: &str) -> &str`
  = note: Varyk imports a returned `&str` or `&S` only from a `&self` method, or from a `pub fn` with exactly one `&T` parameter, when the signature writes no lifetime; otherwise return an owned value, such as `String` instead of `&str`
